;; samples/region.aura
;; Provides a sample region code for the checkout pipeline scenario.
;;
;; The orchestrator (saga/orchestrator.aura) and the tax module
;; (pricing/tax.aura) both expect a region code. We expose a single
;; function, api-sample-region, that returns a region symbol/string
;; the rest of the system recognizes.
;;
;; We pick "US" because the pricing/compute module defaults to it for
;; its embedded tax call, and the stdout contract scenarios in this
;; project are documented around US sales-tax math.
;;
;; Required exported API:
;;   (api-sample-region) -> region-code
;;
;; The returned value is a plain string so it can be passed directly to
;; api-tax-cents (which expects a string) and compared with string=?
;; without any extra conversion step on the caller side.

(define (api-sample-region)
  "US")
